Z||000000||Monkeyman||10-22-2000||10:10 PM||||I have about $3000 to spend on the Grape Ape.  It needs lots of work including the rebuilding of the motor and tranny.  I'll never get rid of the car but I need reliable transportation.  Here's one idea I've been kicking around.  If I could buy a decent fastback (I like the notchbacks better, but the fastbacks have some stock options I want) for less than 3 grand, I could take the time to redo the Grape Ape the right way.  It wouldn't matter if it took a couple of years.<P>Here's what I would have to have in a fastback.  Sunroof, wing, A/C, prefer a stick, gray interior (I hate tan) in good to excellent condition, good suspension, good brakes, working E brake, etc.  Everything would have to work correctly and I'd like no body damage (bad paint doesn't matter).  Wheels/tires don't matter either as I have some aftermarket 15" rims with Pirelli tires on the Grape Ape I could transfer.  I don't want a lot of miles on the motor, either.  I have to be able to rely on a car for the next few years until I can get the Grape Ape finished.<P>I've asked for a lot, but is this even possible or am I dreaming?  If this is possible, let me know and I'll post something in the Mall if I decide to go this route.<P>Thanx for the bandwidth.<BR> <P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||5
